From: Elite eBPF Contrib <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
To: tj@kernel.org, arighi@nvidia.com, peterz@infradead.org
Cc: sched-ext@lists.linux.dev, linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org
Subject: [PATCH] sched_ext: RT-aware watchdog stall detection (sched-ext/scx#1202)

When CPU-intensive RT tasks monopolize a CPU, SCHED_EXT tasks confined to
that CPU cannot proceed. The watchdog currently treats this as
SCX_EXIT_ERROR_STALL and unloads the BPF scheduler — a false positive
when the root cause is RT class priority, not a BPF scheduler bug.

This patch adds RT-pressure detection in check_rq_for_timeouts():

1. Per-CPU kthread exception: if nr_cpus_allowed==1 and rq->curr is RT,
   skip stall check (arighi, sched-ext/scx#1202).

2. Full-mode RT mask check: if NOT partial switch, iterate p->cpus_ptr;
   if any allowed CPU has rt_nr_running==0, the task is genuinely stalled.
   If ALL allowed CPUs have RT tasks, skip stall (RT pressure).

Partial mode (SCX_OPS_SWITCH_PARTIAL) is excluded — FAIR tasks may hog
CPU without RT involvement.

References: https://github.com/sched-ext/scx/issues/1202
Tested: rt_stall + rt_guard_stress kselftests on production server (vmi3469243)

---
 kernel/sched/ext.c | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/ext.c b/kernel/sched/ext.c
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/ext.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/ext.c
@@ -3380,6 +3380,44 @@ static bool scx_partial_switch(void)
 	return static_branch_unlikely(&__scx_switched_all);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Returns true if a runnable stall is likely caused by RT monopolization
+ * rather than a BPF scheduler bug. See sched-ext/scx#1202.
+ */
+static bool scx_stall_caused_by_rt(struct task_struct *p, struct rq *rq)
+{
+	const struct cpumask *mask;
+	int cpu;
+
+	/* Per-CPU kthread starved by RT on this CPU — not a BPF bug. */
+	if (p->nr_cpus_allowed == 1 &&
+	    rq->curr && rq->curr->sched_class == &rt_sched_class)
+		return true;
+
+	/* RT mask check only in full switch mode. */
+	if (scx_partial_switch())
+		return false;
+
+	mask = p->cpus_ptr;
+	if (!mask)
+		return false;
+
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	for_each_cpu(cpu, mask) {
+		struct rq *cpu_rq = cpu_rq(cpu);
+
+		if (cpu_rq->rt.rt_nr_running == 0) {
+			rcu_read_unlock();
+			return false; /* CPU free of RT — genuine stall */
+		}
+	}
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
+	/* All allowed CPUs have RT tasks running. */
+	return true;
+}
+
 static bool check_rq_for_timeouts(struct rq *rq)
 {
 	struct scx_sched *sch;
@@ -3395,6 +3433,13 @@ static bool check_rq_for_timeouts(struct rq *rq)
 		if (unlikely(time_after(jiffies,
 					last_runnable + READ_ONCE(sch->watchdog_timeout)))) {
+			/*
+			 * Skip false-positive stall when RT tasks monopolize
+			 * all CPUs available to this task (sched-ext/scx#1202).
+			 */
+			if (scx_stall_caused_by_rt(p, rq))
+				continue;
+
 			struct scx_dispatch_q *dsq = READ_ONCE(p->scx.dsq);
 			u32 dur_ms = jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - last_runnable);
 
